Subject: [PATCH] R80b, part 6, patch 11 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M16;
 main's third folder, section 2, row A6): B1893'S LOCK HOLDS ITS VERDICT LINE
 AND ITS PAGE BY THEIR SENTENCES

A reader's check of main's answers at Review 80 (agy-002's; row A6, not checked by main). Main wrote that
its wider plants against B1893's lock are caught, and did not make the reader's own. The reader's passes, in
main's words: the verdict line's first 96 characters kept, its count of caught cases turned to none, and the
ten case rows deleted from the page.

Made again here, in a scratch checkout, on the commit before this patch:
  - the verdict line with its first 96 characters kept and the rest replaced: the lock PASSES;
  - the verdict line with every "caught" turned into "not caught": PASSES;
  - the rows of the cases deleted from the page, the first ten or all thirteen: the lock FAILS. As the
    builder made it this one is caught already;
  - the page with "still pass" turned into "ARE REFUSED": PASSES. This is the plant of main's own set that
    was never made (patch 8 of this part); it is made on the words the page has.

The lock held the verdict line by its first 96 characters and its last words. It now holds it by four of its
sentences, refuses a line that says of anything that it is not caught, holds the page by four sentences (the
two bullets of the result, the sentence on the thirteen that still pass, and the note on what the lock
asserts), and holds that "all thirteen" is the run's own count. Five planted changes pass what the lock
asked of the verdict before and are reported now.

On the patch, the same plants in a scratch checkout: each FAILS the lock, and nothing planted passes.

What this does not hold, said here: any other sentence of the page, reworded.

The lock passes: 8 tests. Not checked by main. Tested against planted errors by the session that wrote it.
